==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*2 [[Pigge Victorious|Pigge Victoriouses]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Bang-Bang]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*4 [[Pigge Victorious|Pigge Victoriouses]] spawn after 113.33 seconds<sup>3,400f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*5 [[Pigge]]s spawn after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*2 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]]s spawn after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Bang-Bang]] spawns after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
All of the enemies here have relatively low range so you can use both ranged and melee attackers to fight them off. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] can be used to deal nuke damage to Bang-Bang while area attackers such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]] can be used to clear out the Pigge family.

This is THE ideal stage for Lucky Ticket farming if you don't mind the energy efficiency. Although this stage only yields ~78% tickets compared to the next one (1.4 vs 1.8 on average), you can clear it as fast as 8 seconds. All transition screens will take another ~10s, so it means you can farm it 3 times in a minute, or 250+ tickets per hour.

==='''Strategy 1 (~9s Speedrun)'''===
{{Lineup
|Richest Cat
|Sashimi Cat
|Sushi Cat
|Brah Cats
|Pair Rope Jump Cat
|Maglev Cat
|Awakened Bahamut Cat|30
|notes = *If you do not have the combos, just use any Starting Money Up, Accounting Power Up, or even Worker Cat Start Level Up combos. The difference is only a few seconds.
*A better version is Richest Cat + Accounting Power Up (M) + Starting Money Up (M) which allows you to spawn Awakened Bahamut as soon as the pigge dies, saving less than 1s.
}}

Spawn Maglev, then spawn Awakened Bahamut. Incredibly simple.

It is indeed possible for lv50 Awakened Bahamut to one shot the base with Attack Up (Sm) + (M) combos, but there's only one more slot for a Sm financial combo, resulting in an even longer time.

